# One ignore file, because there is now one build context: the repository root.
#
# The four per-service .dockerignore files are gone. Docker and buildah read
# the ignore file at the CONTEXT root and nowhere else, so the moment the
# context moved out of services/<name>/ those four stopped being consulted —
# leaving four files that look authoritative and do nothing, which is worse
# than none. (BuildKit will also read <Containerfile>.dockerignore beside the
# Containerfile; none of these were named that, so none of them were being
# read under any builder.)
#
# What this file is actually for, in order:
#   1. Keeping packages/common's test tree out of the three images that COPY
#      that directory whole. This is the only line here that changes an image.
#   2. Keeping .git out of the context, which is most of the bytes on the wire.
#   3. Not invalidating a build layer over a file no image contains.

.git

# A workflow edit must not invalidate the pip layer of four builds, and CI
# configuration has no business inside an image.
.github

# The conformance suite runs in CI against the source tree, never from inside
# an image. packages/common is COPYd whole by stt, tts and tts-long, so this
# line is the one that keeps pytest and its fixtures out of a service image.
# Note the package's own README.md and LICENSE are deliberately NOT excluded:
# pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`, and setuptools fails the
# build outright if the file named there is missing from the context.
packages/common/tests

# Not copied by any Containerfile — these lines only keep the context small
# and say plainly what is not build input.
services/*/tests
services/*/conftest.py
services/*/pytest.ini
services/*/requirements-dev.txt

# The benchmark is a client, not part of the service. It has its own
# requirements.txt and pulls a second Whisper implementation.
services/stt/bench

# Models are downloaded into the volume at /models on first start and are
# never baked in — a local models/ directory is gigabytes of context for
# nothing. Same for sample audio.
**/models
**/*.wav

# Deployment, not build input.
compose.yaml

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
